   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone, <div><br></div><div>I&#39;m keen to release an update of the <a href=\"https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357524364000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2oxiXdkRhuzSv302NIgwH0\">RSQLServer</a> package to CRAN in the next few weeks (v0.2). You can read the <a href=\"https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/NEWS.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/NEWS.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357524364000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3aY_mrWO5c6zLnHyXf23jj\">NEWS</a> for what has changed. But the key features are:</div><div><br></div><div>1. An implementation of a SQL backend for dplyr compatibility.</div><div>2. A much better (and backward incompatible) change to the dbConnect interface</div><div>3. Azure-hosted SQL Servers are now supported. </div><div>3. A working example is now provided in the <a href=\"https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/README.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/blob/master/README.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357524364000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3JBl7nSp95WsRTFpu-pPMD\">README</a>. </div><div><br></div><div>For those of you who use this package, could I ask you to install and test this (both the DBI methods and the dplyr support)? Please report any bugs or unexpected behaviour on <a href=\"https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/imanuelcostigan/RSQLServer/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357524364000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dAEkP_0K2P8MjqTD8yrqY\">Github</a>.<br></div><div><br></div><div><div>I am looking to build out a test framework by v0.3.</div></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
